======================================================================================================================
=== PHASE 4i - HOW WIDE IS THE CLOSURE? Continuation conditioned on the STATE, not the clock.
======================================================================================================================
   PURE MEASUREMENT, NOT A POLICY TEST. The elapsed-time family is closed above. The
   question this table answers is whether the NEXT family (a state-dependent stop) has
   anything to aim at: for short trades still open at tau, split by how much unrealised
   profit is on the screen at tau (in units of the entry sigma460), what does the
   remainder of the hold pay? A negative cell is somewhere a stop could live. No rule is
   fitted to this table in this wave and none may be - it is a pointer for a future
   preregistration, and it is DISCOVERY_CONSUMED the moment it is read.

   tau      stat       < -1s      -1..0s       0..1s       1..2s       2..4s        > 4s
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    15         n         382          70          99          74         132         467
       E[fwd] pt        0.65       -4.67       -4.68        5.35        6.80        7.87
         total $       4,965      -6,545      -9,260       7,920      17,945      73,470

    30         n         251          54          47          44          83         426
       E[fwd] pt        6.29       -4.62       -4.60       -1.68       -7.59        9.77
         total $      31,555      -4,995      -4,325      -1,475     -12,605      83,260

    60         n         126          27          25          20          55         309
       E[fwd] pt        9.29       -0.20       -7.29       -2.83       -1.03        8.82
         total $      23,400        -110      -3,645      -1,130      -1,130      54,500

   120         n          67          18          14           4          22         209
       E[fwd] pt       -2.82      -12.81           -           -       16.57        9.07
         total $      -3,785      -4,610           -           -       7,290      37,915

   READ: the biggest bucket at every tau is the DEEPEST-IN-PROFIT one (>4 sigma), and it
   carries the LARGEST POSITIVE continuation at every tau. The intuitive repair - 'a short
   in profit should take it before the bounce' - points the wrong way in this data. The
   negative cells are the thin middle buckets, tens of trades and a few thousand dollars,
   scattered in sign across tau. That is what no signal looks like, not what a stop looks
   like. It does not PROVE the state family is closed - it says nothing in it is obvious.
   The clock is closed; whether the STATE is closed is not settled by this wave and the
   cells above are a description of 2,225 in-sample trades, not a test.

======================================================================================================================
=== PHASE 4h - THE ONE EXCEPTION, AND WHY IT IS NOT A CANDIDATE
======================================================================================================================
   Phase 4f shows every 2026 continuation cell NEGATIVE. Read naively that says 'in the
   sleeve's worst year, cutting the hold would have paid'. That is very close to a
   tautology - in a losing year LESS EXPOSURE OF ANY KIND pays - so the only thing that
   can distinguish information from exposure removal is the state-blind control, run
   INSIDE 2026 and inside the weaker first half.

   --- 2026 only: 182 trades, uncapped $-25,483 at PRIMARY cost
        cap T      REAL $   d vs base    EXP mean     EXP p95  pctile  beats p95
            5     -15,128      10,355     -12,489      -4,808    27.7         no
           15     -11,823      13,660     -16,272      -5,903    76.1         no
           30     -24,708         775     -15,663      -3,349    12.0         no
           60     -13,023      12,460     -12,874        -322    50.0         no
          120        -193      25,290     -13,082      -2,896    98.2        YES
      -> caps beating their own state-blind control at p95: 1 of 5
         5 caps tested and they are near-perfectly nested, so one hit at p95 in a
         182-trade partial year is not evidence; the effective number of
         independent tests here is close to 1-2, and the family-wise expectation
         is not far from the one observed. It is not treated as a signal.

   --- H1 <=2024-02-29: 1115 trades, uncapped $13,820 at PRIMARY cost
        cap T      REAL $   d vs base    EXP mean     EXP p95  pctile  beats p95
            5     -17,835     -31,655     -17,752      -8,054    49.1         no
           15      -9,610     -23,430      -6,217       7,603    35.8         no
           30      13,065        -755         553      16,563    90.8         no
           60      14,160         340       4,650      21,616    82.8         no
          120       8,530      -5,290       8,121      23,828    52.4         no
      -> caps beating their own state-blind control at p95: 0 of 5

   A rule conditioned on 2026 would be fitted to 182 trades in the single worst year the
   sleeve has ever had, chosen AFTER seeing that it is the worst year. The method note
   'never redefine the population after seeing the result' forbids it and this wave does
   not do it. Recorded as a REGIME observation, consistent with W62's finding that the
   sleeve's contribution is regime-shaped - not as a holding-time finding.

